TEAM PROJECT LICENSE AND CONTRIBUTION AGREEMENT

Project Repository: AutoMed
Repository Owner / Group Leader: Jatin

Authorized Team Members:
1. Jatin — Group Leader / Repository Owner
2. Dhairya — Team Member
3. Nikhil — Team Member
4. Akshit — Team Member

Effective Date: 10/10/2026

---

## 1. Purpose of This Agreement

This document governs the use, modification, contribution, and distribution of the AutoMed project repository. It is intended to define the rights and responsibilities of the repository owner, the authorized project team, and any external contributor who may be granted access.

This agreement supplements, rather than replaces, any applicable academic, institutional, legal, or third-party licensing obligations.

---

## 2. Ownership and Repository Authority

This repository was created and is maintained by Jatin, who serves as the designated Group Leader and Repository Owner.

Jatin has primary authority over the GitHub repository, including access controls, branch settings, pull requests, merges, repository permissions, contributor management, and overall project administration.

The repository owner does not automatically claim exclusive ownership of every idea, code contribution, document, design, or work product created by other team members. However, the repository itself remains under the administrative control of Jatin, and all contribution access is governed by the terms of this agreement.

---

## 3. Authorized Team Members

The following individuals are authorized members of this project:

- Jatin — Group Leader / Repository Owner
- Dhairya — Team Member
- Nikhil — Team Member
- Akshit — Team Member

Only the individuals listed above may create, modify, review, or merge project content through the GitHub repository unless explicit written permission is granted by Jatin.

---

## 4. Permission to Modify the Project

Authorized team members may:

- Add, edit, delete, or replace project files
- Write and revise source code
- Create feature branches and submit pull requests
- Fix bugs and improve functionality
- Add documentation and supporting materials
- Review and discuss code and repository changes

Any major changes to the project's architecture, core functionality, or final project direction should be discussed with the Group Leader before merging into the main branch.

---

## 5. Restrictions on Unauthorized Users

The following actions are prohibited for any person who is not explicitly listed as an authorized member of the project:

- Modifying source code
- Creating, deleting, or altering project files
- Making changes in the repository
- Creating branches or pull requests
- Uploading their own version of the project
- Claiming authorship of the project
- Distributing, publishing, or commercializing the project
- Copying substantial portions of the code or project materials for another project

Any person who wishes to contribute to, modify, distribute, or use the project must first obtain explicit permission from Jatin.

---

## 6. External Contributors

If an individual outside the authorized team wishes to contribute, they must:

1. Contact Jatin directly
2. Explain the purpose and scope of the proposed contribution
3. Receive approval before making any changes
4. Follow the repository contribution rules established by the team
5. Obtain final approval before any contribution is merged into the main project

Approval to contribute does not grant ownership, unrestricted rights, or automatic access to project materials.

---

## 7. Main Branch Protection

The main branch is considered the official and stable branch of the project.

Where practical:

- Direct pushes to main should be restricted
- Team members should work in separate branches for significant changes
- Pull requests should be reviewed before being merged
- Jatin has final authority over whether a change is merged into main

---

## 8. Attribution and Credit

All authorized team members should receive proper credit for their work and contributions.

No contributor may remove, alter, or obscure attribution, authorship, or project credit without permission from the Group Leader and the affected contributor.

---

## 9. Academic and Institutional Compliance

This repository is intended primarily for academic and educational project work.

No person may submit this project, or a substantial portion of it, as their own independent work without proper acknowledgment and permission.

All contributors must comply with the academic integrity policies and submission requirements of the relevant institution or course.

---

## 10. Third-Party Materials

Any third-party code, libraries, datasets, frameworks, media, assets, or other materials included in this repository remain subject to the terms of their original licenses.

This agreement does not transfer ownership or rights to third-party materials included in the project.

---

## 11. Confidentiality and Security

Authorized members must not intentionally disclose private project information, unpublished work, design details, credentials, or sensitive repository information to unauthorized parties.

Passwords, API keys, tokens, secrets, and other private credentials must never be committed to the repository.

---

## 12. Repository Access and Account Security

Jatin may grant, modify, or revoke repository access as necessary for project management and team requirements.

Team members must not share their GitHub credentials, authentication tokens, or access privileges with any other person.

Access to the repository is personal and may not be transferred or assigned to another individual without approval.

---

## 13. Modification of This Agreement

This agreement may be revised only through discussion among the authorized team members and approval by the Group Leader.

Changes affecting repository ownership, membership, branch policy, or major rights require approval from Jatin.

---

## 14. Termination of Access

Authorization to modify or access the repository may be removed if:

- A team member leaves the project
- A contributor is removed from the project team
- The person violates project rules or repository policy
- The person creates a security or academic-integrity risk
- The Group Leader determines that access is no longer required

Termination of access does not erase a person's legitimate contribution history or rightful attribution for prior work.

---

## 15. No Unauthorized Redistribution

No person may publish, redistribute, sell, sublicense, or upload the project, or any substantial part of it, to another repository or public platform without permission from Jatin and, where applicable, the other contributors.

---

## 16. Final Authority

For matters concerning the GitHub repository itself, Jatin, as the designated Group Leader and Repository Owner, has final administrative authority over:

- Repository access
- Branch permissions
- Pull requests
- Merging changes
- Repository settings
- Addition or removal of collaborators

This authority does not override the intellectual property rights, ethical obligations, academic requirements, or institutional policies that apply to individual contributors.

---

## 17. Acceptance

By contributing to this repository, the authorized team members acknowledge that they have read and understand this agreement and agree to comply with its terms.

Authorized Team:
- Jatin — Group Leader / Repository Owner
- Dhairya — Team Member
- Nikhil — Team Member
- Akshit — Team Member

